The native_argsort.rs and heap.rs files adapt the libc++ headers listed in
SOURCE.json and heap-provenance.json from the Apple MacOSX27.2 SDK. The exact
header hashes identify the source; this notice does not claim an LLVM commit.

Changes for dinf: safe Rust with checked slices, finite F32 scores, integer
indices, the descending comparator scores[a] > scores[b], and a limit of
128 entries. Guarded stable insertion replaces the small sorts and the
partition-sentinel insertion form. The larger ninther and branchless paths
are excluded. The heap port keeps the arithmetic-index branch and move order.

These files keep their LLVM license terms. dinf's own code keeps its MIT
terms; other component notices remain in force. The scope is this pinned
native ordering, not a platform-independent rule for equal scores.
